contains_on_record.plain, line 3, while running: Check the value of the field "name", or write "has" to check for a field.

    if person contains "Ann"
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    if person's name is "Ann"
  or
    if person has "Ann"
Why: "contains" looks inside text or a list. A record has fields, and "has" checks for a field by its name. "Ann" isn't a field of "person". It's the value of its field "name".
